"><span>Find documents where age is less than or equal to 28 in 'users' col=
lection</span></p><pre><span>db.users.find({ age: { $lte: 28 } })</span></p=
re><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"text-align: justify;"><span>Find documents where=
 title is equal to "MongoDB Overview" in 'posts' collection</span></p><pre>=
<span>db.posts.find({ title: { $eq: "MongoDB Overview" } })</span></pre><p =
dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"text-align: justify;"><span>Find documents where age i=
s not equal to 30 in 'users' collection</span></p><pre><span>db.users.find(=
{ age: { $ne: 30 } })</span></pre><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"text-align: justi=
fy;"><span>In these queries, we utilize the </span><b><strong>$gt</strong><=
/b><span> (</span><b><strong>greater than</strong></b><span>),</span><a hre=
f=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/mongodb/mongodb-less-than-operator-lt/" =
target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener"><b><strong> $lt</strong></b><span> </spa=
n></a><span>(</span><b><strong>less than</strong></b><span>), and </span><b=
><strong>$eq</strong></b><span> (</span><b><strong>equality</strong></b><sp=
an>) comparison operators to filter documents based on specific criteria. A=
dditionally, we demonstrate the $ne (not equal) operator to find documents =
where a field does not match a specified value.</span></p><h3><span>2. Logi=
cal Operators</span></h3><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"text-align: justify;"><spa=
n>Find documents where age is greater than 25 </span><a href=3D"https://www=
.geeksforgeeks.org/mongodb/mongodb-and-operator-and/" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noopener"><span>AND </span></a><span>less than 35 in 'users' collection=
</span></p><pre><span>db.users.find({ $and: [ { age: { $gt: 25 } }, { age: =
{ $lt: 35 } } ] })</span></pre><p dir=3D"ltr" style=3D"text-align: justify;=
"><span>Find documents where username is "johndoe" </span><a href=3D"https:=
